`useEffect` runs after every render by default. You control when it re-runs using the dependency array:

```jsx
// Runs after every render
useEffect(() => { ... });

// Runs only once on mount
useEffect(() => { ... }, []);

// Runs when `value` changes
useEffect(() => { ... }, [value]);
```

Return a cleanup function:

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  const timer = setInterval(() => console.log('tick'), 1000);

  return () => clearInterval(timer); // cleanup on unmount
}, []);
```

React calls this before the component unmounts or before the effect runs again.
